{"id": "sonnet__GEN__omni_1884__0", "result": "The smallest such n is 8.\n\nLet P(n) = 1!\u00b72!\u00b7\u00b7\u00b7(n\u22121)! and R(n) = P(n)/(n!)\u00b2. We want the smallest n with R(n) > 1.\n\nSince P(n+1) = P(n)\u00b7n!, the ratio satisfies\n\nR(n+1) = R(n)\u00b7n!/(n+1)\u00b2.\n\nStarting from R(1) = 1 (empty product over 1), we get:\n\n- R(2) = 1\u00b71/4 = 1/4\n- R(3) = (1/4)\u00b72/9 = 1/18\n- R(4) = (1/18)\u00b76/16 = 1/48\n- R(5) = (1/48)\u00b724/25 = 1/50\n- R(6) = (1/50)\u00b7120/36 = 1/15\n- R(7) = (1/15)\u00b7720/49 = 48/49 < 1\n- R(8) = (48/49)\u00b75040/64 \u2248 77.1 > 1\n\nSo R(n) \u2264 1 for n \u2264 7 and R(8) > 1.\n\nANSWER: 8", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.013571999999999999, "model_used": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "secs": 13.0}